          ZERO-INIT BUG (project-wide lesson): fresh array[N] of int
          comes back with dirty heap memory here (measured 1.4e9-range
          values in a brand-new array[6]), so every partially-written
          alloc is a landmine.  It bit as cards[2..5] garbage, which
          made the red-lock check pass without a card (door opened on
          first use).  Fix: explicit zeroarr() loops in playerreborn
          for all five Player arrays + Floor.texture/newspecial and
          Plat.count at spawn.  Audited remaining game.b allocs:
          tmbbox/spechit/scrolllines guarded by counts, thinker/mobj
