          NUMERIC VALIDATION FIRST (/tmp/opencode/shoot_oracle.py):
          true-DDA vanilla walk transcribed from p_maputl.c (MAPBLOCK
          SHIFT 23/BTOFRAC 7, saturating FixedDiv incl. INT_MIN edge,
          origin<<16, boundary nudge) over E1M1 BLOCKMAP vs the port
          formulation, both with exact finesine table.  Oracle caught
          TWO real engine bugs before any edit: (1) collectshoot used
          P_PointOnLineSide (trace ends vs line) where vanilla uses
          P_PointOnDivlineSide (line ends vs trace) for all traces
          longer than 16u (all shooting + use) — the functions differ
          in both the sign-bit fast path and >>8 vs >>16 rounding;
          corner-graze rays picked the neighboring wall (line 4@1447
          vs vanilla line 1@1448, same outcome kind, 1 frac apart).
          Fixed with the vanilla long/short branch (mirrors slidetrace)
          + pointondivside delegated to pointondvlineside; (2) oracle's
          own cell-index and div-saturation bugs found by the same
          battery (map-vs-fixed unit mixup, wrapping fdiv_c, INT_MIN
          off-by-one).  AFTER the fix: 109/109 AGREE (16 spawn dirs +
          16 use-range + aimed pistol/melee at a zombie + 64 courtyard
          dirs with a zombie + elevated imp; plus a positive-slope
          autoaim case 36327 exact both sides).  uselines deliberately
          UNCHANGED: its LineSide formulation misses some later
          intercepts vs vanilla (23/64 use dirs) but first-hit — the
          only thing its nearest-first oof/use walk consumes — agrees
          64/64 and the M13 exit harness passed end-to-end; the
          329/330/331 cluster tuning stays as validated.
