          M10 FOLLOW-UP, TWO USER REPORTS (both confirmed real):
          (1) dead enemies block movement: NOT a bug — vanilla-faithful.
          P_KillMobj clears MF_SOLID for players only (p_inter.c:703
          is inside `if (target->player)`), PIT_CheckThing has no
          corpse exemption, so monster corpses block XY movement in
          real Doom too (must walk around; height>>=2 only lets shots
          and missiles pass OVER, via the slope/z windows already
          validated).  BUT the report exposed a REAL divergence
          underneath: vanilla clears corpse solidity mid-death-
          animation via A_Fall ("actor is on ground, it can be walked
          over", p_enemy.c), fired from exactly one frame in every
          monster death/xdeath sequence (zombie DIE3/XDIE3, imp
          DIE4/XDIE4, demon DIE4, caco DIE5, baron DIE4...), while our
          doaction no-op left corpses solid FOREVER.  Fix: ACT_FALL
          index resolved from inf->actnames at init; doaction handles
          A_Fall by clearing MF_SOLID (first live A_* action; M11/12
          table still to come).  Barrels have no A_Fall frame and stay
          solid in both.  Validated headless (TEMP hooks removed
          after): SPECTEST12 PASS — fresh zombie corpse solid at
          death, clear lands exactly on DIE3 entry (state 189+2, whose
          table action resolves to A_Fall), ~death+8 within slop,
          player walks through the fallen cell (dist 9), barrel
          corpse still solid after 40 tics.  Harness-only lessons:
          kill-shot thrust shoves live targets AND corpses, so track
          victims by ref not coords; the harness needs its own
          `load Info` + `inf->init()` (module loads are per-instance —
          the view.b lesson in the porting notes bit again: constants
          work, variables come back empty).
          (2) can't shoot above/below the plane: real gap — interim
          firepistol hardcoded slope 0 and never called the (already
          implemented) autoaim.  Fix: firepistol now mirrors vanilla
          P_BulletSlope exactly (straight aim, then +-1<<26 retries,
          MISSILERANGE) and passes the slope to plineattack (first-shot
          exact aim like P_GunShot accurate=true; flash/ammo/refire
          spread stay M11).  Validated headless: SPECTEST11 PASS —
          victim 64 above: engine aim slope +14873 == oracle vanilla
          walk to the unit, damaged 20->5; player 64 up shooting down:
          slope -23979 exact, victim 5->-1.  Below-plane math was
          already oracle-covered both directions (negative slopes in
