          USER-REPORTED RENDER BUG (doomsnap0-5, E1M1 nukage pool):
          two symptoms, opposite verdicts.
          (1) NUKAGE NOT ANIMATING: real engine bug, fixed.  Root
          cause was architectural, not the anim math (which was
          vanilla-exact and now measured cycling 50,52,51-exact):
          anims/nanims/texanim/flatanim were Rend MODULE globals,
          but module loads are per-instance — doom.b's Renderer.init
          ran animinit on instance D, the game ticker advanced
          instance G (anims==nil -> silent early-out), and view.b
          read instance V (flatanim nil -> raw flat).  Three ships in
          the night; flats never animated (same freeze hit wall
          texture anims).  Fix: tables moved onto the shared Renderer
          adt (rend.m fields; adt travels with the rr handle across
          modules), animtic(r, lvltime) now ticked by doom.b after
          game->ticker() (the sim never holds rr).  Validated
          end-to-end (TEMP harness removed after): full view render
          of the pool overlook, 614 window bytes differ across 8
          tics, zero differ after 24 tics (exact 3-frame cycle
          closure — rules out stand-frame flips, which are 20-tic).
          Lesson for the porting notes: module globals are
          per-load-instance; shared mutable state belongs on adts
          passed by handle (rr/game pattern), never on modules.
          (2) 1-COLUMN NUKAGE STRIPE (x=124, snaps 1-5; x=100/89,
          snap0): VERDICT vanilla-faithful slime-trail artifact, no
          code change.  Exhaustive analysis: the stripe is the pool
          plane (NUKAGE3, sector 57 floor -48) showing through rows
          where the neighbor columns show sector-60 brown
          (FLOOR5_2, floor -24).  Per-column replay with engine-exact
          math (scale bases from the snapshot DS records, WAD
          heights/textures, camera) reproduces the framebuffer
          exactly: at x=124 the far platform-top 1S wall (ld=269,
          ~716u, visited first per BSP order) terminally closes the
          column before the nearer 57|60 boundary wall (ld=182,
          ~200u) can mark sector-60's floor, so only the pool mark
          ([118,200], laid earlier by the platform front ld=201)
          survives; at x=123 the boundary wall marks brown first
          ([134,200]) and the pool mark stops at its top edge.
          Every link verified against doomgeneric source: BSP walk
          order (R_RenderBSPNode + R_CheckBBox prune is perf-only),
          1S terminal close (r_segs.c: ceilingclip=h, floorclip=-1),
          mark gating/windows (r_segs.c:315,345 + 219+), span merge
          and plane draw order — all decision-identical, so vanilla
          renders the byte-identical stripe at this vertex-exact
          column.  Deliberately NOT "fixed": clamping 1S closes to
          drawn rows would diverge from vanilla and break the
          snapshot-validated sprite-clip model.  The imp alignment
          in the snaps is viewpoint coincidence (imp stands on the
          platform behind the boundary vertex).  Snap0 x=89 is
          ordinary wall-edge texel variation, not the same defect
          (no cross-column run).
          FOLLOW-UP (user disputed vanilla-faithful + recent):
          pushed much harder.  Bisection via headless warp-render
          harness (TEMP, outside repo): stripe present in EVERY
          testable build back through Oct 13 (6e097f45) — spanning
          pre-gating, pre-near-plane-snap, pre-shut-skip, pre-view-
          gates, pre-per-column-light code.  Predates all recent
          work (M13/M10/A_Fall/autoaim/anim touched only game.b/
          sound.m/doom.b/rend.b; the anim fix postdates the snaps).
          Mechanism nailed to the frame level and cross-checked
          against the snapshot's own drawseg records (solid evolution
          + mark strips match exactly): far platform-top 1S wall
          (ld=269, ~716u) closes column x=124 before the nearer
          57|60 boundary wall (ld=182, ~200u) can mark sector-60's
          brown floor, so the pool plane (marked [118,200] by the
          platform front ld=201 beforehand) fills rows the brown
          floor owns (134-199 verified geometrically: x=124 ray
          enters sector 60 at ~199u, floor -24 owns rows 134+).
          Visit order independently confirmed by replaying E1M1's
          BSP walk in Python (subsector 163 before 177, matching
          the engine DS order) — no walk bug.  Every link matches
          doomgeneric source (walk incl. no-prune equivalence,
          1S terminal close r_segs.c, mark gating r_segs.c:315/345,
          span merge, creation-order plane draw, clip init,
          duplicate rule R_CheckPlane, FixedMul int64 semantics);
          pointonside-vs-R_PointOnSide disagreement tested: zero
          on all E1M1 nodes, all snapshot cameras, full play-area
          sweep.  So: present since the renderer first drew this
          scene, vanilla-correspondent at every checkable link —
          slime-trail class.  No code change (a "fix" would break
          the validated terminal-close/sprite-clip model).  Honest
          residual: vanilla parity is by source-equivalence +
          bisection, not side-by-side execution (no vanilla binary
          here); a vanilla screenshot differing at this spot
          reopens it.  Working theory for "recent": the artifact is
          viewpoint-specific (vertex-exact column) and only became
          visible with F1 snapshot-freezing + recent playtesting of
          new areas — not a code regression.
