          PERF PASS (no milestone; user-reported "solid but slow"):
          headless bench (TEMP, removed) showed the loop at ~50ms/
          frame vs the 28ms 35Hz budget — tick itself 0.07ms, render
          ~38ms (walls/planes pixel loops in Limbo), convert ~11ms
          (64k palette map) — so the old blocking tick chan starved
          the sim to ~17 game-tics/sec: slow motion, not low fps.
          Fixes, all behavior-identical (bench checksums match before/
          after on 3 views): tick/render decoupling with ticdup-style
          catch-up (tick chan buffered [8], drain all owed ticks per
          frame, cap 4; ticcmd rebuilt per ticker so turn ramp stays
          exact; game time now tracks wall time at 35 tps), wall
          top/bottom texture lookup hoisted out of the per-column loop
          (was a 125-entry string scan per column), drawplanes row-
          major span emission (same span set; drops the per-plane
          array[h] alloc and the per-column close-scan), rdrawcolumn
          power-of-2 row-mask fast path (100/125 TEXTURE1 heights are
          128), rclear via pre-zeroed slice copy (was a 64k loop).
          F2 review ring gated behind doom -R (default off; per-frame
          fb+clip copy ~1ms + masked scans; F1 snapshot unaffected —
          it reads the live frame).  After: E1M1 start 33ms/frame
          (~30fps, planes 14ms/walls 8-10ms/convert 11ms), spin view
          28ms, wall-closeup 21ms; game speed real-time even where
          frames drop.  Residuals: per-pixel loops + convert are the
          floor in Limbo (needs the M24 blockmap for tick-side scale
          and, if more fps wanted, per-column big-op fast paths or
          half-rate rendering).
